-- title:
--   Sub-lattices of type m are the primitive ones of index N²
-- statement:
--   Let $a,b\in\mathbb{Q}$ and let $\Lambda_1$ be a $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of the quaternion algebra $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ which is a maximal order, i.e. it contains $1$, is closed under multiplication, spans $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ over $\mathbb{Q}$, is finitely generated, and is the largest submodule with these four properties among those containing it. Let $N$ be a nonzero natural number and let $m$ be a unit of $\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]\otimes_{\mathbb{Q}}\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$, where $\mathbb{A}_{\mathbb{Q}}^{\mathrm{fin}}$ is the finite adele ring of $\mathbb{Q}$ and [`Submodule.finiteAdeleBox`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L14) $\Lambda_1$ denotes the additive subgroup generated by the elements $z\otimes\alpha$ with $z\in\Lambda_1$ and $\alpha$ a finite adele integral at every height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_{\mathbb{Q}}$. Assume: $m$ lies in that box; $N\cdot m^{-1}$ lies in that box; and the submodule $\Lambda_1\cap(\mathrm{conjByFiniteIdele}\ \Lambda_1\ m)$, consisting of those $z\in\Lambda_1$ whose image $z\otimes 1$ lies in $m\cdot(\text{box})\cdot m^{-1}$, has relative index $N$ in $\Lambda_1$ as additive subgroups. Let $x,g$ be further units with $g$ in the box. For a unit $h$, write $\Lambda_1(h)$ for [`Submodule.ofFiniteIdele`](def/Submodule_FiniteAdeleBox.html#L19) $\Lambda_1\ h$, the $\mathbb{Z}$-submodule of those $z\in\mathbb{H}[\mathbb{Q},a,b]$ with $z\otimes 1\in h\cdot(\text{box})$. Then there exists $u$ in the stabiliser of the box (as a set) under left translation by units, with $\Lambda_1(xg)=\Lambda_1(xum)$, if and only if $\Lambda_1(xg)$ has relative index $N^2$ in $\Lambda_1(x)$ and, for every prime $p$, $\Lambda_1(xg)$ is not contained in $p\cdot\Lambda_1(x)$.
--
--   This is the elementary-divisor dictionary for lattices over an Eichler order: under the hypotheses on $m$ (integral, with $Nm^{-1}$ integral and the associated intersection of index $N$), the right sub-lattices of $I_x=\Lambda_1(x)$ obtained from $x$ by the adelic type $m$ are characterised intrinsically as the primitive sub-lattices of index $N^2$, equivalently of reduced norm $N$. It is used in the Čerednik–Drinfeld part of the development, where such sub-lattices are matched with cyclic subgroups of order $N$ and the resulting kernel ideals.
